update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The skills and knowledge imparted in the basic instruction must be deepened and updated in regular training. Special importance must be attached to the thorough gathering, documentation, and interpretation of the measuring results. | For seizing the results of operating methods, regular training courses (e. g. annually) are necessary. [...] Essential components of regular training courses must therefore include the following points: proper use of pipettes and their regular check, selection of suitable test kits and measuring ranges, regular check of the equipment used such as thermoreactors and photometers, qualified and regular use of IQC-Cards. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.3.2 / §4.3.3, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-012; gate is homed on worksheet -03 although successive_supervision_interval and training_courses_attended live on worksheet -04 (mis-home, STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='4381d61d-4bbb-451b-91cd-162b1b9fc0a1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- application_mode  [ATV-A-704E-03]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For the reasonable application of operating methods the following guidelines apply: When pertaining to water and wastewater fee regulations, operating methods can only replace reference methods if this is regulated by law. [...] The use of operating methods can clearly reduce the need for reference methods. So, for example, in self-monitoring - except for the parallel analysis - reference methods can be omitted. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.1, printed p.11) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.7; caveat: §4.1 does not define a three-way mode taxonomy; the enum value "single_substitute" has no printed basis - the word "substitute" does not occur anywhere in the Standard (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='18a2e2ea-bac0-49f2-b652-a0169313a048' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- expected_concentration_range  [ATV-A-704E-03]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='By referring to the criteria mentioned in Sections 3.1 and 3.2, the operator must decide for the operating method that is suitable for his specific case of application. In doing so, especially the measuring range must be selected in such way that preferably the expected result can be found in the 20 % to 80 % interval of the measuring range. From experience, this range shows the greatest analytical reliability. Suitable dilution steps are permitted. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.2, printed p.11) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.7; caveat: field is data_type number with a single unit mg/l and therefore cannot hold the interval the clause is about (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='b54bae59-2316-4b50-9dea-bb155f5c7e73' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- method_selected_suitable  [ATV-A-704E-03]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='By referring to the criteria mentioned in Sections 3.1 and 3.2, the operator must decide for the operating method that is suitable for his specific case of application. In doing so, especially the measuring range must be selected in such way that preferably the expected result can be found in the 20 % to 80 % interval of the measuring range. From experience, this range shows the greatest analytical reliability. Suitable dilution steps are permitted. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.2, printed p.11) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.7', verified_at=now() where id='59c933e1-7f6d-44b5-8703-5c88de1a87ad' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- validation_range_coverage_pct  [ATV-A-704E-03]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='By referring to the criteria mentioned in Sections 3.1 and 3.2, the operator must decide for the operating method that is suitable for his specific case of application. In doing so, especially the measuring range must be selected in such way that preferably the expected result can be found in the 20 % to 80 % interval of the measuring range. From experience, this range shows the greatest analytical reliability. Suitable dilution steps are permitted. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.2, printed p.11) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.7; FINDING: the field description asserts "at least 80 % of the measuring range is covered when validating against the reference method". No such rule is printed. §4.2 constrains WHERE THE EXPECTED RESULT falls (the 20 % to 80 % interval of the measuring range) - a two-sided window, not a one-sided coverage minimum. Invented specification (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='c6dfbb6d-7a52-409d-b4b9-0989e5a99391' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- basic_instruction_done  [ATV-A-704E-04]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='An intensive basic instruction must be carried out according to the following factors: overview of the parameters to be analysed, introduction to parameter-specific sampling including the required pre-treatment of samples and preservation, practice of the operating method for each parameter with representative wastewater samples of the planned cases of application (autonomous completion and handling) according to the given work instruction, — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.3.1, printed p.11) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.7', verified_at=now() where id='a14367b7-d2d0-432a-9548-599748b8dc73' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- successive_supervision_interval  [ATV-A-704E-04]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The skills and knowledge imparted in the basic instruction must be deepened and updated in regular training. Special importance must be attached to the thorough gathering, documentation, and interpretation of the measuring results. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.3.2, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: §4.3.2 prints NO interval ("regular training" only); the field is is_required=true and demands a value the Standard never states (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='118d561d-2848-49a4-95c4-47714f2e1b83' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- training_courses_attended  [ATV-A-704E-04]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For seizing the results of operating methods, regular training courses (e. g. annually) are necessary. [...] Essential components of regular training courses must therefore include the following points: proper use of pipettes and their regular check, selection of suitable test kits and measuring ranges, regular check of the equipment used such as thermoreactors and photometers, qualified and regular use of IQC-Cards. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.3.3, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: is_required=false although §3.3 lists "c) regular training measures" inside a must-clause and §4.3.3 says regular training courses "are necessary"; "e. g. annually" is an EXAMPLE, not a printed interval (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='ef889e28-2cd7-4c7d-bbac-eab7a7a350bf' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_05_cr_014  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='When using operating methods, the operator must pay special attention to quality control (see also Annex A). This ensures that the handling, the reagents used and the measuring equipment are checked regularly as follows: check of the reproducibility of a sample by multiple determination, measuring of standard solutions to check the procedure, the measurement equipment and reagents, parallel analyses as a comparison to reference methods, [...] check of plausibility by dilution and standard addition of the wastewater sample, [...] control of the reagents'' storage life. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-014', verified_at=now() where id='c1f3bb54-9438-44c7-8d02-e7d1abd5ed19' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_05_cr_015  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='In most cases, the user of operating methods will carry out the sampling/pre-treatment of samples him-/herself. This is why an introduction to the importance of sampling, the problems related to it, the selection of suitable sampling equipment and the sample containers as well as the transport of samples and pre-treatment of samples must be given. [...] The sampling and pre-treatment must be documented (e. g. in the operation log). — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.5 Sampling and Preservation, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-015; the gate''s stored source_quote is only the first, DESCRIPTIVE sentence ("In most cases, the user ... will carry out the sampling ... him-/herself"), which carries no obligation - the obligations are the two following sentences quoted here; the gate is also homed on worksheet -05 although worksheet -06 is "Probenahme & Konservierung" (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='07035276-46e5-4710-a430-3abe5ad79b85' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- sample_suitability_checked  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='This ensures that the handling, the reagents used and the measuring equipment are checked regularly as follows: check of the reproducibility of a sample by multiple determination, — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: symbol and label say "sample suitability" but §4.4 bullet a) is about REPRODUCIBILITY by multiple determination; bullets a) and b) are crossed between this field and multiple_determination_performed (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='f0ca0816-39a7-4d13-8561-f90749071c21' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- multiple_determination_performed  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='measuring of standard solutions to check the procedure, the measurement equipment and reagents, — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: symbol says multiple determination but the stored description quotes bullet b) (measuring of standard solutions). §4.4 bullet b) - the IQC-Card 4 measure - has no correctly-named field of its own (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='e4582093-3bc7-4666-a220-64fdae15f25e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- parallel_analysis_performed  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='parallel analyses as a comparison to reference methods, — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: is_required=false although bullets a) to g) all sit under the same "the operator must pay special attention to quality control" (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='65b56c25-a42c-4c67-ae25-5b91c1e70f2e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- equivalency_check_performed  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='equivalency measurements by means of operating methods from other wastewater systems (e.g. within the scope of wastewater treatment plant neighbourhoods) and/or participation in interlaboratory tests, — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: is_required=false although bullets a) to g) all sit under the same must-clause (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='c13c4553-6799-4be9-8c1b-64851355f670' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- blank_and_standard_controlled  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='check of plausibility by dilution and standard addition of the wastewater sample, — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4, printed p.12) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; FINDING: the symbol, label ("Blindwert & Standard kontrolliert") and description invoke a BLANK VALUE. "Blank value"/"Blindwert" as an analytical control appears NOWHERE in DWA-A 704E; §4.4 bullet e) is "check of plausibility by dilution and standard addition of the wastewater sample" and the encoding also drops "dilution". Invented specification (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='61869740-fe2d-4faf-a4a3-c33d1c8e2594' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- reagent_storage_life_controlled  [ATV-A-704E-05]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='control of the reagents'' storage life. | Control of the storage life of the reagents: Usually, the reagents have a storage life of 2 years if stored in a dry, dark and cool place. Only few tests have a reduced storage life, 12 and/or 18 months, or must be stored refrigerated. The expiry date is given on the packing. [...] Quarterly, the stock should be checked and all expired sets should be disposed of. — printed p.12 and 55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§4.4 / IQC-Card 9, printed p.12 and 55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8', verified_at=now() where id='57ab3556-d842-4d11-b25f-b09661da2e12' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- sample_type  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The sampling of a wastewater sample can be carried out as single, random, qualified random or mixed sample: Single sample: A random (with reference to time and/or location) sample gained by single taking (mostly by scooping) from a body of water. | Random sample: One or several single samples taken in subsequent order to analyse the current condition. | Mixed sample: Two or several samples or semi-samples that are continuously taken and mixed in an adequate ratio in order to determine the average value of a certain parameter. | Qualified random sample: Special type of a mixed sample consisting of at least five random samples that are taken within a period of maximally two hours in intervals of not less than two minutes and are mixed. — printed p.49', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8, printed p.49) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27; caveat: the printed name of the fourth type is "Qualified random sample", encoded as "Qualified sample"; the printed definition also carries three numeric constraints (at least five random samples, maximally two hours, intervals of not less than two minutes) that no field and no gate captures (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='7e9db805-3f93-4971-ac1e-115111cf7f0d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- sampling_method  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 8 - Sampling, Sampling Log, Method of sampling: manual sampling [ ] - automatic sampling [ ] time proportional [ ] volume proportional [ ] flow proportional [ ] — printed p.51', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8 Sampling Log, printed p.51) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.28; FINDING: the printed log is TWO independent axes - manual/automatic, and (for automatic) time-/volume-/flow-proportional - as five separate checkboxes; the encoding flattens them into ONE single-select, so "automatic + flow proportional", the normal filled state in the printed example (p.53), cannot be recorded (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='ce0015fe-7560-4ba3-a931-53e6fbaeae4c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- storage_temperature  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Storage of samples: What is the optimum storage temperature to eliminate changes of the sample in the best possible way? The wastewater sample should be stored at temperatures around 4 °C for a short time. In this way, for instance, the bacterial conversion of ammonium to nitrate can be suppressed. — printed p.49', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8, printed p.49) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27; caveat: the printed value is "around 4 °C"; the field description instead says "as cold as possible, e.g. refrigerator", a wording that is not printed, and omits the 4 °C entirely (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='51ccb057-80bb-4234-9b35-db48cb902a4f' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- max_storage_time  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Storage of samples: What is the optimum storage temperature to eliminate changes of the sample in the best possible way? The wastewater sample should be stored at temperatures around 4 °C for a short time. In this way, for instance, the bacterial conversion of ammonium to nitrate can be suppressed. | Besides the current measuring results, all boundary conditions must be documented. Among those are time (or period), type and location of the sampling, type and duration of the storage, measures for pre-treatment (e. g. preservation) of the sample, information on the method of analysis, etc. — printed p.49 and 13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8 / §5.1, printed p.49 and 13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27; caveat: the Standard prints NO maximum holding time - only "for a short time" (p.49) and the duty to document "type and duration of the storage" (§5.1). The field name asserts a maximum the source does not define (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='2bd018cd-8540-4de6-b8e8-4e335cd0b68f' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- container_material  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Which container material is suitable for sampling? Changes of the sample due to interactions with the container material must be eliminated. | Were the containers thoroughly cleaned before the re-use and were flushed with fully desalinated water? Sample enrichment/carry-over by pre-flushing with contaminated water or wastewater residues must be prevented. — printed p.49', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8, printed p.49) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27', verified_at=now() where id='f33700f7-7bd8-4c78-81d0-303d64e27e58' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- precipitation_influence  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 8 - Sampling, Sampling Log: Pre-treatment: none [ ] cooled [ ] added: ______ | Influence of precipitation: yes [ ] no [ ] — printed p.51', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8 Sampling Log, printed p.51) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.28; FINDING: the printed Sampling Log offers a BINARY "Influence of precipitation: yes [ ] no [ ]". The encoded enum {none, partial, full} invents "partial" and "full" and renames "no" to "none". Invented enum values (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='6db12eeb-5b19-4aff-af84-5a9cef4bec58' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- sample_pretreatment  [ATV-A-704E-06]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Pre-treatment of the samples: Is a homogenisation of the sample urgently necessary and/or reasonable? [...] The homogenisation is carried out according to DIN 38402-30 if not regulated otherwise. | Is a filtration of the sample before the photometrical measurement necessary or possible? [...] Is a thermal-chemical digestion necessary? [...] Is a dilution of the sample necessary? If the measurement range is exceeded, the sample must be diluted and/or another measurement range must be used. — printed p.49-50', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 8, printed p.49-50) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.28; caveat: clause_reference §A.4 points at the Sampling Log (printed p.51), whose printed pre-treatment options are "none / cooled / added: ____" - a different taxonomy with a free-text branch; the encoded 4-value enum is drawn from the p.49-50 narrative instead and drops the printed "none" (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='b79ca86b-0030-4908-8581-5847b05ccf1c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_07_cr_016  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Taking into account the above listed notes on quality control is a prerequisite for correct analysis results of a constant high quality. However, the data only achieves an adequate meaning if the circumstances of their survey and the further measures taken for quality assurance are documented in a suitable form, e. g. by means of IQC-Cards. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.1, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-016', verified_at=now() where id='f9563141-9b08-4003-a397-a860d617f796' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_07_cr_017  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='All measures described under Item 4.4, which are carried out for quality control, must be documented concisely and extensively. This especially enables the operating staff and external staff to gain an objective impression of the quality of the collected data. The documentation can, for instance, be performed in the form of IQC-Cards, which record each quality control measure. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.2, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-017', verified_at=now() where id='248db68d-c974-47be-92fb-c20e6eaf154e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_07_cr_018  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Within the scope of the documentation, a constant up-to-date overview of the staff''s qualification as well as of the participation in regular training measures should be kept. This allows the proof that measurements or sampling were carried out by qualified staff. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.3, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; attestation checkbox for gate CR-018; the clause is "should be kept" - CR-018 is a BLOCK gate anchored on soft text (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='ff1c8b3e-8277-4883-9597-995b0e49b64e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- results_documented  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The measuring result must make a representative statement for the case of application. When quoting measuring results, if possible, only few digits should be used. Generally, two significant digits are quoted, e. g. 0.24; 2.4; 24, 240; 2400. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.1, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8; caveat: the printed rounding rule ("Generally, two significant digits are quoted") has no field and no gate (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='abe52567-7d53-40b2-9cee-81fdefc9d065' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- quality_control_documented  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='All measures described under Item 4.4, which are carried out for quality control, must be documented concisely and extensively. This especially enables the operating staff and external staff to gain an objective impression of the quality of the collected data. The documentation can, for instance, be performed in the form of IQC-Cards, which record each quality control measure. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.2, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8', verified_at=now() where id='e2efb34f-1bb6-42fa-b2df-0d9e51b60813' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- qualification_documented  [ATV-A-704E-07]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Within the scope of the documentation, a constant up-to-date overview of the staff''s qualification as well as of the participation in regular training measures should be kept. This allows the proof that measurements or sampling were carried out by qualified staff. — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (§5.3, printed p.13) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.8', verified_at=now() where id='72794274-1b6e-40ce-8ce8-2c5ac1c3fb9e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_08_cr_020  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Internal specifications allow the user to define individual quality targets (Section 4.4). The DWA Working Group IG-4.3 recommends minimum frequency, tolerances and quality targets (Sheet 1 of IQC-Card 2). The individual target should be documented in Sheets 2 and 3 of IQC-Card 2. The internal specifications should match the recommendations and could certainly be tightened. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2, printed p.22) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; attestation checkbox for gate CR-020; the clause reads "recommends", "should match", "could certainly be tightened" and sits inside Annex A, which A.1 (printed p.16) declares "not of a regulating kind but of a recommending one" - CR-020 is a BLOCK gate on soft text (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='af3a3051-ed84-4ab9-8290-8c3da05bd341' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_08_cr_021  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 - Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3, col.3 Minimum frequency: Multiple determinations 1x per month, person- and matrix-related | Measurement of standards after each 10th sample; at least 1x per month, person-related | Plausibility checks (spiking, dilution) if measuring results are implausible; if matrix changes; 1x per quarter | Equivalency measurements and/or interlaboratory test (operating methods) 1x per year, person-related | Parallel measurements to the reference method 1x per year, method-related | Pipettes 100-1000 µl volume check 4x per year | pH-meter check 1x per month | Heating device/thermoblock check 1x per year — printed p.23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1, printed p.23) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; attestation checkbox for gate CR-021; the table is headed "Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3" and Annex A.1 (printed p.16) declares the Annex "not of a regulating kind but of a recommending one" - CR-021 is a BLOCK gate on a recommendation table (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='d2962b47-f2a8-44a8-9ba4-230dbb094259' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_08_cr_024  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 - Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3, col.4 Quality target: Multiple determinations Random error < 10 % * | Measurement of standards Adherance to the permissible value range (control limits) | Plausibility checks (spiking, dilution) deviation < 20 % * | Equivalency measurements Deviation < 20 % * | Parallel measurements to the reference method Deviation < 20 % * | Pipettes 100-1000 µl Deviation < 2 % | Pipettes > 1000 µl Deviation < 1 % | pH-meter Deviation < 0.2 pH | Heating device/thermoblock Deviation < 3 °C | * For measuring results in the lower concentration range (e. g. Ptotal < 1 mg/l) greater percental tolerances are possible. In this case their permissible deviations should be defined in mg/l. — printed p.23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1, printed p.23) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; attestation checkbox for gate CR-024; same recommendation table as CR-021 - BLOCK gate on soft text (STAGED). The printed targets are STRICT ("< 10 %", "< 20 %") while the gates that consume them (CR-019/022/023) use <=', verified_at=now() where id='13bfcb3c-a803-47d8-9567-45de5d028c6e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- attest_atv_a_704e_08_cr_027  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Monitoring of the photometer: Within the scope of testing equipment monitoring, the function of photometers must be tested regularly. The device must be checked annually according to the instructions manual. The test kit can be ordered as a test solution kit from the manufacturer of the photometer. The entire optical system of the photometers is checked. The monitoring must be documented on Sheet 1. — printed p.55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30; attestation checkbox for gate CR-027; the gate is homed on worksheet -08 although photometer_check_done and the rest of the IQC-Card 9 fields live on worksheet -11 - the gate reads no field of its own worksheet (mis-home, STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='99317415-207c-4e2d-92af-83e788db77b3' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- qa_measure  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 - Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3, col.1 Quality assurance measure: Multiple determinations | Measurement of standards | Plausibility checks (spiking, dilution) | Equivalency measurements and/or interlaboratory test (operating methods) | Parallel measurements to the reference method | Pipettes 100-1000 µl volume check | Pipettes > 1000 µl volume check | pH-meter check | Heating device/thermoblock check | Measuring device check (e.g. photometer) — printed p.23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1, printed p.23) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; the 9 enum values map onto the 10 printed rows (the two pipette rows collapse into one value)', verified_at=now() where id='47a1e4dc-056a-4cda-8758-8a76a24c4ba8' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- qa_quality_target_pct  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 - Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3, col.4 Quality target: Multiple determinations Random error < 10 % * | Measurement of standards Adherance to the permissible value range (control limits) | Plausibility checks (spiking, dilution) deviation < 20 % * | Equivalency measurements Deviation < 20 % * | Parallel measurements to the reference method Deviation < 20 % * | Pipettes 100-1000 µl Deviation < 2 % | Pipettes > 1000 µl Deviation < 1 % | pH-meter Deviation < 0.2 pH | Heating device/thermoblock Deviation < 3 °C | * For measuring results in the lower concentration range (e. g. Ptotal < 1 mg/l) greater percental tolerances are possible. In this case their permissible deviations should be defined in mg/l. — printed p.23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1, printed p.23) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; FINDING: the field description states "pipettes 100-5000ul <2%, >1000ul <1%" and "plausibility <20% / <25% lower range". The printed row is "Pipettes 100-1000 µl"; neither "5000" nor "25 %" occurs anywhere in DWA-A 704E. Invented values. The printed targets also include non-percentage units (< 0.2 pH, < 3 °C) and an mg/l branch for the lower concentration range, none of which a single %-unit field can carry (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='54a8027e-aac1-4208-88bd-79c65309ac03' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- survey_measure_count  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='To be able to recognise all performed quality assurance measures for a wastewater system quickly and reliably, a survey card must be produced. In a structured way it documents the overall measures that were taken within a certain period of time - similar to an annual report. [...] The information on the number of measures taken is therefore only entered at the end of this period. [...] To receive a relation of the IQC-measures taken for the samples analysed, also their number must be given. — printed p.18', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 1, printed p.18) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; prose-only quote carrying no numeric value, rests on the OCR alone', verified_at=now() where id='907e7397-3c3b-4f23-8a5d-b97ce9ee7197' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- qa_minimum_frequency  [ATV-A-704E-08]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 - Recommendations by the DWA-Working Group IG-4.3, col.3 Minimum frequency: Multiple determinations 1x per month, person- and matrix-related | Measurement of standards after each 10th sample; at least 1x per month, person-related | Plausibility checks (spiking, dilution) if measuring results are implausible; if matrix changes; 1x per quarter | Equivalency measurements and/or interlaboratory test (operating methods) 1x per year, person-related | Parallel measurements to the reference method 1x per year, method-related | Pipettes 100-1000 µl volume check 4x per year | pH-meter check 1x per month | Heating device/thermoblock check 1x per year — printed p.23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1, printed p.23) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.14; caveat: printed as recommended minimum frequencies inside the recommending Annex A; is_required=true (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='9ee02f74-41df-4110-a248-234e2e4e288e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- single_result_i  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 3 - Multiple Determinations (form header): 1 Date | 2 Name | 3 Sample designation | 4 Measured value 1 [mg/l] | 5 Measured value 2 [mg/l] | 6 Measured value 3 [mg/l] | 7 Mean [mg/l] | 8 Greatest spread Difference [mg/l] | 9 Greatest spread Col 8 x 100% / Col 7 [%] | 10 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? — printed p.30', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 3, printed p.30) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.18; printed form columns 4-6 "Measured value 1/2/3" in mg/l', verified_at=now() where id='406332df-549f-4c5a-ba1a-ede23a996dce' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- n_determinations  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Usually it is sufficient to carry out a double determination of the sample to be analysed. A triple determination additionally increases the analytic reliability of the measuring results and should be carried out for greater variations in the measured values. — printed p.29', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 3, printed p.29) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; prose-only quote carrying no numeric value, rests on the OCR alone; the Standard prints "double"/"triple" determination; no fixed n is mandated', verified_at=now() where id='70d941fc-ffee-43c4-bab7-514ece5e0d8e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- mean_value  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='From the single results a mean value must be produced, which represents the measuring result. Here, all single results must be included in the mean. | From the single measured values the mean (add single measured values and divide them by the number of the measured values; column 7) is produced. | IQC-Card 3 - Multiple Determinations (form header): 1 Date | 2 Name | 3 Sample designation | 4 Measured value 1 [mg/l] | 5 Measured value 2 [mg/l] | 6 Measured value 3 [mg/l] | 7 Mean [mg/l] | 8 Greatest spread Difference [mg/l] | 9 Greatest spread Col 8 x 100% / Col 7 [%] | 10 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? — printed p.29 and 30', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 3, printed p.29 and 30) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.18', verified_at=now() where id='bdaa6d20-d635-4e89-aea2-7c7696f6752e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- deviation_single_pct  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The greatest difference in the single measured values is entered into the IQC-Card in mg/l (column 8) and in % (greatest difference of the single measured values divided by the mean value; column 9). In column 10 the result of the control measure is documented. | IQC-Card 3 - Multiple Determinations (form header): 1 Date | 2 Name | 3 Sample designation | 4 Measured value 1 [mg/l] | 5 Measured value 2 [mg/l] | 6 Measured value 3 [mg/l] | 7 Mean [mg/l] | 8 Greatest spread Difference [mg/l] | 9 Greatest spread Col 8 x 100% / Col 7 [%] | 10 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? — printed p.29 and 30', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 3, printed p.29 and 30) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.18; FINDING: printed column 9 is the GREATEST SPREAD (greatest difference of the single measured values x 100 / mean, form p.30 "Col 8 x 100% / Col 7"). The encoded EQ-02 computes a SINGLE value''s deviation from the mean - a different, systematically smaller statistic - and CR-019 gates on it (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='a15431cb-4712-48f4-b2af-fcaf439e080d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- control_measure_value  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The greatest difference in the single measured values is entered into the IQC-Card in mg/l (column 8) and in % (greatest difference of the single measured values divided by the mean value; column 9). In column 10 the result of the control measure is documented. — printed p.29', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 3, printed p.29) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.18; caveat: the p.29 text says "In column 10 the result of the control measure is documented", but the rendered form on p.30/31 prints column 10 as "Interpretation: Quality target achieved?" - the Standard''s text and its own form disagree; the encoding follows the text', verified_at=now() where id='a03e984b-8643-4a53-8239-bd1090247982' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
