-- calculated_value  [ATV-A-704E-09]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 5, Sheet 1 - Dilution: 2. Single steps: a) Determination of the MEASURED VALUE ORIGINAL SAMPLE (column 3) b) Dilution c) Determination of MEASURED VALUE DILUTED SAMPLE (column 5) | 3. Formulas for calculation: DILUTION FACTOR (column 4) = TOTAL VOLUME / SAMPLE VOLUME. CALCULATED VALUE (column 6) = DILUTION FACTOR · MEASURED VALUE DILUTED SAMPLE | If the variation between CALCULATED VALUE and MEASURED VALUE ORIGINAL SAMPLE is smaller than given in the internal specification (IQC-Card 2), there is no error in the matrix. If it is greater, an error in the matrix is likely. — printed p.35', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 5 Sheet 1, printed p.35) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.20; FINDING: calculated_value is consumed by no equation and no gate. The printed Sheet 1 form (p.37) carries "Deviation absolute Col6-Col3" and "Deviation relative Col7 x 100/Col3", and IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 sets the plausibility target at deviation < 20 % - none of that is encoded, so the plausibility check is the one printed QA measure with no gate at all (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='d23d3cb4-2c81-44d4-ae25-4274c84a0b6c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
