-- deviation_equivalency_pct  [ATV-A-704E-10]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 6 - Equivalency Measurements (form header): 1 Date | 2 Name | 3 Sample designation | 4 Parameter | 5 Mean [mg/l] | 6 Nominal value or mean of the equivalency measurements [mg/l] | 7 Deviation of the mean from the nominal value [mg/l] | 8 Deviation relative [%] | 9 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? | Usually, the deviation in the central measurement range should not exceed the quality target of < 20 % (in this regard also see IQC-Card 2: Internal Specifications). — printed p.45 and 43', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 6, printed p.45 and 43) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.25; FINDING: the printed worked example on p.45 marks -23.3 % and -20.7 % as "no!" against "Defined permissible deviation in %: 20", i.e. the printed rule is on the MAGNITUDE of the deviation. Gate CR-022 encodes deviation_equivalency_pct <= qa_quality_target_pct over a SIGNED value, so both of the Standard''s own failing rows would pass. Two-sided printed tolerance encoded one-sided (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='2e7fc789-7602-4443-b176-39513f19f9d4' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- measured_value_reference  [ATV-A-704E-10]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 7 - Parallel Measurements to the Reference Method (form header): 7 Referenced monitoring Measured value [mg/l] | 8 Measured value of the operating method [mg/l] | 9 Deviation absolute Col8-Col7 [mg/l] | 10 Deviation relative Col9 x 100/Col7 [%] | 11/12 Permissible deviation Condition [mg/l] [%] | 13 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? — printed p.48', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 7, printed p.48) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27', verified_at=now() where id='b24a020b-a5e9-41d2-8109-051d1c375130' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- deviation_parallel_pct  [ATV-A-704E-10]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 7 - Parallel Measurements to the Reference Method (form header): 7 Referenced monitoring Measured value [mg/l] | 8 Measured value of the operating method [mg/l] | 9 Deviation absolute Col8-Col7 [mg/l] | 10 Deviation relative Col9 x 100/Col7 [%] | 11/12 Permissible deviation Condition [mg/l] [%] | 13 Interpretation: Quality target achieved? | Usually, the deviation in the central measuring range should not exceed the quality target of < 20 % (see also IQC-Card 2 in this regard: Internal Specifications). Especially with measuring results in the lower concentration range (e. g. Ptotal < 1 mg/l) greater percental tolerances are possible. — printed p.48 and 46', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 7, printed p.48 and 46) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.27; FINDING: the field description says "in % (IGC-Card 7 column 9); also recorded as absolute deviation (column 10)". The printed form has it the other way round - column 9 is the ABSOLUTE deviation (Col8-Col7, mg/l) and column 10 the RELATIVE one (Col9 x 100/Col7, %). Gate CR-023 has the same signed-value defect as CR-022 (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='b614440a-dd7d-404d-b640-cffadefa6942' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- testing_equipment  [ATV-A-704E-11]
