-- monitoring_interval  [ATV-A-704E-11]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='IQC-Card 9: Recommendations for control- and monitoring frequencies can be taken from the table. | Testing equipment / Monitoring: BOD-respirometer biannually | Photometer annually | Annealing furnace annually | Heating device/thermoblock annually | Ion exchange annually | Piston stroke pipettes quarterly | Refrigerator annually | Conductivity measuring device biannually | pH-meter monthly | Sampling equipment biannually | Reagents quarterly | Oxygen measuring device every two weeks | Thermometer quarterly | Thermo cabinet annually | Drying cabinet annually | Scales annually — printed p.54', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.54) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30; caveat: the printed table BINDS one interval to each equipment item; the encoding lets any equipment be paired with any interval and no gate enforces the printed pairing (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='0909584f-951a-4850-be78-15411a3f3597' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- pipette_tested_volume  [ATV-A-704E-11]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The mean must be calculated from the 5 results of the weightings. [...] The mean value must lie within a defined tolerance range (see table). | Tested volume [ml] / Deviation [%] / Tolerance range [g]: 0.100 / ≤ 2 / 0.098 - 0.102 | 0.200 / ≤ 2 / 0.196 - 0.204 | 0.500 / ≤ 2 / 0.490 - 0.510 | 1.000 / ≤ 1 / 0.990 - 1.010 | 2.000 / ≤ 1 / 1.980 - 2.020 | 5.000 / ≤ 1 / 4.950 - 5.050 | If the results lie outside the tolerance range, the pipette must no longer be used as testing equipment (remove designation) and should be sent to the manufacturer for testing, if necessary. — printed p.55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30; the six volumes named in the field description match the printed rows exactly', verified_at=now() where id='8909a6d7-43e0-4bfb-9c6e-00311216790c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- pipette_deviation_pct  [ATV-A-704E-11]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The mean must be calculated from the 5 results of the weightings. [...] The mean value must lie within a defined tolerance range (see table). | Tested volume [ml] / Deviation [%] / Tolerance range [g]: 0.100 / ≤ 2 / 0.098 - 0.102 | 0.200 / ≤ 2 / 0.196 - 0.204 | 0.500 / ≤ 2 / 0.490 - 0.510 | 1.000 / ≤ 1 / 0.990 - 1.010 | 2.000 / ≤ 1 / 1.980 - 2.020 | 5.000 / ≤ 1 / 4.950 - 5.050 | If the results lie outside the tolerance range, the pipette must no longer be used as testing equipment (remove designation) and should be sent to the manufacturer for testing, if necessary. — printed p.55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30; FINDING (SR-2, needs a ruling): IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 (printed p.23) sets "Pipettes 100-1000 µl ... Deviation < 2 %" and "Pipettes > 1000 µl ... Deviation < 1 %", which puts 1000 µl = 1.000 ml at < 2 %; this IQC-Card 9 table puts 1.000 ml at <= 1. The two printed tables DISAGREE at exactly 1000 µl - not auto-picked. Gate CR-025 also leaves 0.5 ml < v < 1.0 ml satisfying neither branch, so a 0.7 ml pipette can never pass a BLOCK gate (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='d97d389e-0670-4ba2-a5c8-6b17c5aceed4' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- heating_device_deviation  [ATV-A-704E-11]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Monitoring of heating device/thermoblock: Within the scope of testing equipment monitoring, the function of thermoblocks must be checked annually. Check of the required temperatures of 100 °C and/or 148 °C (± 3 °C). Alternatively, also other/further frequently used temperatures can be tested. — printed p.55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30; FINDING: the printed tolerance is TWO-SIDED (± 3 °C at 100 °C and/or 148 °C); gate CR-026 encodes heating_device_deviation <= 3 one-sided, so -5 °C passes. IQC-Card 2 Sheet 1 also prints the target as strict "< 3 °C" while the gate uses <= (STAGED)', verified_at=now() where id='bc460338-0d82-4948-bf3a-44989434e95c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- photometer_check_done  [ATV-A-704E-11]
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Monitoring of the photometer: Within the scope of testing equipment monitoring, the function of photometers must be tested regularly. The device must be checked annually according to the instructions manual. The test kit can be ordered as a test solution kit from the manufacturer of the photometer. The entire optical system of the photometers is checked. The monitoring must be documented on Sheet 1. — printed p.55', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 (IQC-Card 9, printed p.55) [VA-OCR]; source is OCR of a scanned PDF with no text layer; image-confirmed on the rendered page PDF p.30', verified_at=now() where id='6f6668ce-7581-4137-ba22-13e99be1f017' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
